      <li><strong>Officially permitted:</strong> the line’s own policy permits it, subject to its published requirements.</li>
      <li><strong>Conditionally permitted:</strong> the line’s own policy says it may be approved case by case or only in certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Not permitted:</strong> the line’s own policy says it is not offered from its ships.</li>
      <li><strong>Unverified:</strong> we found no official policy. This is not a “no.” It means you need to ask the line in writing.</li>
    </ul>
